AUDIO: 'The colors were also too strong and oversaturated. So, at first, I used RGB as a channel mode. RGB carries the color details from your reference image and sometimes this'

[05:49] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'adds too much color and makes the final image look fake. And to fix this, go to the create to control image and code node. Change the channel mode from RGB to gray'

[06:01] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'scale. Here, gray scale removes the color information from control image. And this allows the model to focus only on depth, pose, and composition.'

[06:13] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Next, change your normalization setting to per image min max. This setting makes the closest areas of the depth map brighter and the distant areas darker.'

[06:27] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'This gives the model a clear understanding of what is close and what is far away. If you don\'t normalize your depth map correctly, the AI can easily get confused.'

